Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::a_fill_succeeds_exactly_when_every_reply_is_full`.

The defect: `fill_with` refuses only a reply that delivers more than it asked for, and accepts a
short one. The standard library's caller accepts partial counts on purpose; this function promises
the opposite, and the defect quietly leaves bytes in the slice that the service never sent.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `result.is_some()` against every reply being
full, with one reply short.

